      "rationale": "This is a secondary, lower-priority observation about a width-specific generate branch. Given how narrow and rare the triggering pointer pattern is (only 1 out of 8 possible low-bit values, only at the near-full boundary, only at one specific non-default width), this is considered a lower-confidence, possibly benign burst-timing optimization for the WIDTH=24 bus profile rather than the primary concern in this design. The reset-logic redundancy above is considered more broadly impactful and thus the primary finding.",
